{"q":"560","t":"Subarray Sum Equals K","d":"Medium","p":false,"c":"<p>Given an array of integers <code>nums</code> and an integer <code>k</code>, return <em>the total number of subarrays whose sum equals to</em> <code>k</code>.</p>\n\n<p>A subarray is a contiguous <strong>non-empty</strong> sequence of elements within an array.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong class=\"example\">Example 1:</strong></p>\n<pre><strong>Input:</strong> nums = [1,1,1], k = 2\n<strong>Output:</strong> 2\n</pre><p><strong class=\"example\">Example 2:</strong></p>\n<pre><strong>Input:</strong> nums = [1,2,3], k = 3\n<strong>Output:</strong> 2\n</pre>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li><code>1 &lt;= nums.length &lt;= 2 * 10<sup>4</sup></code></li>\n\t<li><code>-1000 &lt;= nums[i] &lt;= 1000</code></li>\n\t<li><code>-10<sup>7</sup> &lt;= k &lt;= 10<sup>7</sup></code></li>\n</ul>\n","h":["Will Brute force work here? Try to optimize it.","Can we optimize it by using some extra space?","What about storing sum frequencies in a hash table? Will it be useful?","sum(i,j)=sum(0,j)-sum(0,i), where sum(i,j) represents the sum of all the elements from index i to j-1.\r\n\r\nCan we use this property to optimize it."],"m":"{\n  \"name\": \"subarraySum\",\n  \"params\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"nums\",\n      \"type\": \"integer[]\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"k\",\n      \"type\": \"integer\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"return\": {\n    \"type\": \"integer\"\n  }\n}\n","g":[{"name":"Array","slug":"array"},{"name":"Hash Table","slug":"hash-table"},{"name":"Prefix Sum","slug":"prefix-sum"}],"s":[{"t":"Two Sum","s":"two-sum","d":"Easy","p":false},{"t":"Continuous Subarray Sum","s":"continuous-subarray-sum","d":"Medium","p":false},{"t":"Subarray Product Less Than K","s":"subarray-product-less-than-k","d":"Medium","p":false},{"t":"Find Pivot Index","s":"find-pivot-index","d":"Easy","p":false},{"t":"Subarray Sums Divisible by K","s":"subarray-sums-divisible-by-k","d":"Medium","p":